    "tool": "save_document",
    "arguments": {
      "title": "Comgu resolution: NH-BREW-PRO commerce parity (58fec068)",
      "content": "Comgu run `58fec068329646719a7110c8db7c0e27` resolved 6 commerce contradiction(s) caused by a change to `NH-BREW-PRO`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Authoritative source: `urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:shopify,northstar_home.catalog.products,PROD)`\n- Price: 109.00 USD\n- Sellable inventory: 3\n- Return window: 30 days\n\n## What was wrong\n\n- **Merchant feed advertises a stale price** (critical) on `urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:s3,northstar_home.feeds.google_merchant_feed,PROD)`\n  - expected `109.00`, observed `89.00`\n  - Shoppers see 89.00 in Shopping ads and free listings, then are charged 109.00 at checkout.\n- **Bundle can oversell available inventory** (critical) on `urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:postgres,northstar_home.bundles.bundle_availability,PROD)`\n  - expected `3`, observed `5`\n  - Up to 2 customers can complete checkout for stock that does not exist, and their orders must be cancelled after payment.\n- **Promotion is anchored to a stale price** (high) on `urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:postgres,northstar_home.promotions.promotions_active,PROD)`\n  - expected `109.00`, observed `89.00`\n  - The advertised sale price of 75.65 is calculated from a price the store no longer charges.\n- **AI shopping manifest is stale** (high) on `urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:s3,northstar_home.ai.shopping_manifest,PROD)`\n  - expected `{'price': '109.00', 'available': 3}`, observed `{'price': '89.00', 'available': 12}`\n  - Third-party shopping agents quote these values directly to shoppers, so the wrong price and stock level are stated as fact before the customer ever reaches the store.\n- **Customer-facing asset has no owner in DataHub** (medium) on `urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:s3,northstar_home.ai.shopping_manifest,PROD)`\n  - expected `at least one owner`, observed `none`\n  - Errors on this surface persist until someone notices, because no team is accountable for it.\n- **Storefront return policy contradicts the authoritative policy** (medium) on `urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:postgres,northstar_home.policy.storefront_policy,PROD)`\n  - expected `30`, observed `14`\n  - Customers are told they have 14 days to return this item when they actually have 30.\n\n## How it was resolved\n\nComgu generated a patch from registered remediation templates and validated it: 7 tests passed, 0 failed.\n\nApproved by amir@comgu.site. Comgu never mutates a downstream system without a recorded human approval.\n\n## For whoever comes next\n\nThese surfaces project from the authoritative catalog. If you change price, inventory or policy at the source, expect every asset listed above to need re-derivation \u2014 pinned values in their configs will not follow automatically.",
